    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0062_14d8209c7cf4.jpg\" style=\"height: 117px; width: 280px;\" /><br /><br />When the string jerk tight both particles begin to move with velocity components <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math> in the direction <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> . Using conservation of momentum in the direction <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math><br /><br />or <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Hence, the velocity of ball <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> just after the jerk is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  }
}